---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'; import ProductImage from '../components/ProductImage.astro'; import { href } from '../lib/paths';
const groups=[
 ['Interactive Workbench','workbench','Arrange an experiment around a physical model.','Connect the source, transmission line and load, position non-invasive probes, and use popup component editors with explicit engineering settings. The line length belongs to its physical model; moving a symbol does not change it.','Predict how a supported physical change will affect the result before explicitly running a Manual workbench.','workbench'],
 ['Four-Channel Oscilloscope','oscilloscope','Read the same solution through four channels.','Assign connected voltage measurements to CH1–CH4, use Time/Div and Volts/Div, select a valid trigger and inspect numerical measurements and cursors. Waveforms are reconstructed from the steady-state analytical solution.','Connect physical phase relationships to waveforms while respecting valid-frequency, bandwidth and trigger diagnostics.','oscilloscope'],
 ['Plot Studio','plot-studio','Move between local readings and scientific curves.','Inspect current spatial, time, frequency and supported parameter curves. Use scientific axes, cursors and comparisons; export the current permitted graph as CSV or PNG.','Compare your expectation with a visible current result. Plots are not a measurement recorder or a simulation-run history.','plot-studio'],
 ['Transmission-Line Simulation','wave-propagation','Study propagation within an explicit scope.','Use distributed RLGC, lossless, lossy and distortionless models with supported source/load contracts. Equivalent canonical section chains are supported; arbitrary non-equivalent junction networks are not.','Investigate matching, ideal open/short loads, attenuation and standing waves with the right assumptions.','result-validity'],
 ['Experiment Library & Experiment Builder','experiment-library','Structure the learning, not just the circuit.','Choose one of five built-in experiments or author portable educational templates. Preconfigured, Equipment Ready and Empty starts serve different learning goals. Instructor-controlled visibility keeps protected theory distinct from legitimate measurements.','Use guided questions and deliberate reveal. Hidden Throughout Exercise stays hidden after Reveal Results.','experiment-builder'],
 ['Local Projects and Offline Workflow','workbench','Keep your work in explicit local files.','Save project configuration in .wavelab and experiment templates in .wavelab-exp. Supported earlier formats migrate through validation. Manual projects reopen as Run Required; a calculated recording is not implied.','Continue a local investigation without a mandatory application account. Windows/WebView2 servicing and GitHub remain separate services.','projects'],
];
---
<Base title="A focused virtual transmission-line lab" description="Explore the six implemented capability groups in RBE WaveLab, from physical workbench connections to real analytical measurements and current scientific plots." path="features/"><div class="container"><header class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Capabilities</span><h1>Tools for asking<br/>better engineering questions.</h1><p class="lede">A coherent desktop workflow, built around transmission-line experiments and the interpretation of physical results.</p></header><div class="section">{groups.map(([title,image,lead,body,value,guide],i)=><section class="split feature-row"><div><span class="feature-index">0{i+1} / CAPABILITY</span><h2>{title}</h2><p class="lede">{lead}</p><p>{body}</p><p>{value}</p><a href={href(`learn/guides/${guide}/`)}>Read the practical guide →</a></div><ProductImage id={image}/></section>)}</div><div class="callout warning"><h2>Know the model's boundaries.</h2><p>V1 is not a general transient/branched-circuit simulator or physical acquisition tool. There is no FMI runtime, automatic history recorder or automatic application updater. <a href={href('scientific-scope/')}>Read the authoritative scientific scope</a>.</p></div></div></Base>
